# Pike: the forms war.
dialogue pike
  node halt pike "Halt! Quarantine station. No admittance without a Bill of Health. Fumigated, stamped, countersigned and dated."
    note pike_bill "Pike's gate opens for a Bill of Health, nothing else. It must be fumigated, stamped, countersigned and dated. He beamed when he said no."
    -> beams
  node beams narrator "He beams at me. It's the look of a man who has waited his whole life to say no to somebody."
    -> love
  node love pike "I love this job."
    > "Where would I get a Bill of Health?" if not has bill -> need
    > "What does a Bill of Health need, exactly?" if has bill -> need
    > "What's regulation six?" if seen:pike.need and not bill_dated -> six
      set pike_reading
    > "Who's in quarantine?" -> who
    > "Do you like it here, Pike?" if not seen:pike.like -> like
      add aff 1
    > "Good day, Pike." -> bye
  node again pike "Sir! Back already. Is it paperwork? Please say it's paperwork."
    > "Where would I get a Bill of Health?" if not has bill -> need
    > "What does a Bill of Health need, exactly?" if has bill -> need
    > "What's regulation six?" if seen:pike.need and not bill_dated -> six
      set pike_reading
    > "Who's in quarantine?" -> who
    > "Do you like it here, Pike?" if not seen:pike.like -> like
      add aff 1
    > "Good day, Pike." -> bye
  node need pike "Every captain carries blanks. Fumigated at my brazier, stamped by a harbour officer, countersigned, dated. Rules three to six."
    > "What's regulation six?" if not bill_dated -> six
      set pike_reading
    > "Does anyone ever manage all four?" -> four
  node four pike "Stamped, lots. Signed, often. But you'd be amazed how many forget the date, sir. Everybody, is how many."
    > "What's regulation six?" if not bill_dated -> six
      set pike_reading
    > "I'll bear it in mind." -> bye
  node six narrator "Pike closes his eyes. He lifts his chin. He puts one hand on his heart. It's the posture of a man who has saved this for a very long time."
    -> recite
  node recite pike "“Regulation six. The Dating of Bills. Six, a: every bill bears the date on the station calendar, kept in the hut, which is mine. Six, b…”"
    -> drone
  node drone narrator "There are a great many letters after b, by the sound of it. His eyes are shut. His hut is open. I've taken a step toward it."
  node who pike "Sailors, sir. Six crews. Very sick. They look well, but that's the illness. It's ever so sneaky."
    > "Who says they're sick?" -> says
    > "I see." -> bye
  node says pike "The form, sir. Cray and Company, quarantine dues paid in full. You can't argue with paid in full. I've tried. It just says it again."
  node like pike "I do, sir. Everyone else I worked for shouted. Here there's a form for everything. Fill it in and things happen. Nobody does, mind."
    -> like2
  node like2 narrator "Behind me, Quill makes a small noise. In anyone else I'd call it sympathy."
  node bye pike "Good day, sir! Come back with your paperwork. I'll be here. I'm always here."
  # The finished bill (rooms_act3.ts, key_gate).
  node passed narrator "He reads it twice, moving his lips. Then once more with his finger."
    -> four2
  node four2 pike "Fumigated. Stamped. Countersigned. Dated."
    -> tear
  node tear narrator "He wipes his eye with the corner of his armband."
    -> beautiful
  node beautiful pike "It's beautiful. Nobody ever does the dating."
    > "Thank you, Pike." -> open
    > "Will you have it framed?" -> framed
  node framed pike "Better than framed, sir. Memorised. I'll be saying it to myself at night."
    -> open
  node open narrator "He hands the bill back, reluctantly, like a man returning a puppy."
    -> gate
  node gate pike "Gate's open, sir. Keep it on you. Inspections are random. Mind the Weather Works. They're not a form sort of people."
    -> thread
  node thread pike "Past them it's the camp. Six crews, pending. One of them's a captain who keeps asking me for thread."
    -> walk
  node walk narrator "Thread. I don't say anything. I notice I've started walking."
  # Talking to Pike again at the open gate.
  node held pike "Still open, sir. I keep checking. Mind the Weather Works. If you see the captain, I've no thread. I've looked."
  # In the salt camp, after the halyard (rooms_act3.ts, salt_camp scene).
  node landed narrator "We land in a salt pan in a heap, in a spray of white. When I can see again, Pike is standing over us. He has run all the way round."
    -> rope
  node rope pike "Arrival by rope! Arrival by rope is not an approved means of entry, sir!"
    -> bearer
  node bearer pike "You're all right, sir. You're inspected, you've a bill. But she hasn't. Unaccompanied cargo is held pending inspection."
    -> goes
  node goes quill "Cargo. He called me cargo. …Fine. I'll go quietly. Clerk? This is your department."
    -> locked
  node locked narrator "She lets him walk her to the store hut. It frightens me more than the Weather. The padlock clicks. Pike looks at his clipboard and stops."
    note quill_held "Pike has locked Quill in the store hut as unaccompanied cargo, pending inspection. She says it's my department. It is."
    -> camp
  node camp pike "Camp duty, sir. It's very like gate duty, only more people are sad at me."
    > "What would release her?" if not knows_form9 -> nine
    > "Pike, I need you to look the other way." if not seen:pike.twelve -> twelve
    > "About the Form 9." if knows_form9 -> how
    > "Who are all these people?" -> crews
    > "Never mind." -> sorry
  node nine pike "A Form 9, sir. Release of Detained Person Upon Inspection."
    -> none
  node none pike "Only we haven't got any Form 9s. We've never had any Form 9s. Nobody's ever been released."
    > "Then I'll write one." -> write
      set knows_form9
      note form9 "Form 9: Release of Detained Person Upon Inspection. Written clean and stamped by a harbour officer. Any paper will do. Pike has none."
    > "Nobody? In three years?" -> nobody
  node nobody pike "Not once, sir. I did wonder. But wondering isn't a form."
    > "Then I'll write one." -> write
      set knows_form9
      note form9 "Form 9: Release of Detained Person Upon Inspection. Written clean and stamped by a harbour officer. Any paper will do. Pike has none."
  node write pike "You can't just write a form, sir."
    -> can
  node can narrator "I'm a clerk of the Port Vela customs house. Writing forms is the only thing I can just do. All I need is paper, and the stamp."
  node how pike "A proper Form 9 is written clean and stamped by a harbour officer, sir. On any paper. Even the back of something."
  node twelve pike "There's a form for that too, sir. Form 12. We haven't got any of those either."
  node crews pike "Six crews, sir, raking salt. Pending inspection. Some of them have been pending a very long time."
  node sorry pike "Sorry about the lady, sir. It's nothing personal. It's regulations, which is worse."
  # Form 9 (rooms_act3.ts, salt_camp).
  node form9 narrator "Pike reads Form 9 with his finger, mouthing the long words."
    -> real
  node real pike "That's… that's a real form."
    -> plural
  node plural pike "Release of Detained Persons. Persons, sir. With an s."
    > "Yes. I wrote it in the plural." -> everybody
    > "Is that a problem?" -> everybody
  node everybody narrator "He looks out at six crews of sailors, all raking, all pending. You can watch the sum arrive on his face."
    -> inspected
  node inspected pike "…That's everybody, sir. (He blows his whistle.) Inspection's over! Everybody's… everybody's inspected!"
    -> rakes
  node rakes narrator "A hundred and thirty rakes stop. Pike unlocks the hut. Quill comes out, salt on her shoulders. She looks at the form, then at me."
    -> wrote
  node wrote quill "You wrote a form."
    > "I wrote a very good form." -> kiss
    > "I'd have written a hundred." -> kiss
      add aff 1
  node kiss narrator "She takes my face in both hands, salt and all, and kisses me. I hold on. I've been told to keep doing that."
    -> ansel
  node ansel ansel "Ah. Good. I'll come back."
    -> turn
  node turn narrator "A sunburnt man with a needle in his lapel and a flag under his arm stops. He turns to go. He turns back. He drops the flag."
    talk ansel
  # Talking to Pike after he's been out-formed.
  node done pike "I've filed it, sir. In my hat. It's the safest place on the key."
    -> roll
  node roll pike "…And this, sir. The roll. Every name on the key, all six crews. I kept it neat. I'd like it to go somewhere it'll be read."
    set pike_roll
    -> roll2
  node roll2 narrator "Six ships' worth of names in a hand so careful it's almost shy. I put it in the log, where they belong."
    -> bright
  node bright pike "Is this what being on the right side feels like, sir? It's very bright."
    > "Customs is hiring. We have a great many forms." -> hiring
    > "You did well, Pike." -> well
  node hiring pike "(whispering) Do you have a Form 12?"
  node well pike "Did I, sir? Nobody's ever said. I'll write it down before it wears off."
  # Pike, once he's handed over the roll.
  node after pike "Still filed, sir. The roll's with you and the form's in my hat. Between us we're very well organised."
    > "Customs is hiring. We have a great many forms." if not seen:pike.hiring -> hiring
    > "Carry on, Pike." -> END
